WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.558 --> 00:00:15.379
the boys were eager to ride Hurry.

2
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.782
The ostrich traveled unbelievably quickly from Rockburg to Falconhurst.

3
00:00:20.523 --> 00:00:23.365
His speed led the boys to quarrel over who should own him.

4
00:00:24.385 --> 00:00:26.527
So I had to step in and end the arguing.

5
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.069
"Hurry belongs to Jack," I said.

6
00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:33.832
"Jack weighs less than Fritz or Ernest, so he is more suited to ride the bird.

7
00:00:34.684 --> 00:00:37.867
And Franz is not yet strong enough to manage such a fast animal."

8
00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:39.928
Fritz started to protest.

9
00:00:39.948 --> 00:00:43.411
"But Father—" "And," I continued.

10
00:00:43.892 --> 00:00:46.333
"Jack was the one who captured him and named him.

11
00:00:47.154 --> 00:00:49.696
But you may all practice riding him occasionally.

12
00:00:50.537 --> 00:00:52.598
And anyone may ride him in an emergency."

13
00:00:52.618 --> 00:00:54.880
"Thank you, Father," said Jack.

14
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.222
"But you must make me some goggles.

15
00:00:58.063 --> 00:01:02.546
Sometimes Hurry goes so fast that I have to shut my eyes to protect them from the wind."

16
00:01:03.347 --> 00:01:04.348
"Really?" I said.

17
00:01:04.828 --> 00:01:06.289
"I must do no such thing."

18
00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:07.710
"Why not?"

19
00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.471
Jack looked at me with amazement.

20
00:01:10.211 --> 00:01:13.273
"First because you cannot tell me I 'must' do anything.

21
00:01:14.154 --> 00:01:17.756
And second because you are perfectly capable of making goggles yourself."

22
00:01:18.797 --> 00:01:21.719
"I guess I do need an indoor activity," said Jack.

23
00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:25.081
Indeed our outdoor activities were coming to an end.

24
00:01:26.021 --> 00:01:30.064
Great black clouds and violent storms marked the beginning of another rainy season.

25
00:01:30.848 --> 00:01:34.930
Rockburg was a more spacious and pleasant place to spend the winter than Falconhurst.

26
00:01:35.791 --> 00:01:37.892
And we had many activities to keep us busy.

27
00:01:40.053 --> 00:01:41.874
Still the time dragged for all of us.

28
00:01:41.894 --> 00:01:45.156
"Let's build a kayak," said Fritz one day.

29
00:01:45.176 --> 00:01:49.759
"I've often longed for a more manageable boat than the canoe or the sailboat."

30
00:01:49.779 --> 00:01:51.439
"Oh yes, Father!"

31
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.320
pleaded Ernest.

32
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.502
"I've read about the kayaks that people build in Greenland."

33
00:01:56.442 --> 00:01:59.224
All the boys were immediately enthusiastic about the idea.

34
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.040
But my wife was not.

35
00:02:01.061 --> 00:02:07.003
"'Your chances of drowning are already great enough with the canoe and the sailboat," she declared.

36
00:02:07.023 --> 00:02:10.684
"This is going to be a very safe boat," I reassured her.

37
00:02:11.545 --> 00:02:14.746
We started our boat-building by constructing a frame of whalebone.

38
00:02:15.646 --> 00:02:18.808
Then we used bamboo to strengthen the sides and build the deck.

39
00:02:19.588 --> 00:02:23.930
That covered the whole length of the boat, leaving only a small square hole to sit in.

40
00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.291
We were totally caught up in our work.

41
00:02:27.251 --> 00:02:30.384
By the time the kayak was complete, the rainy season was over.

42
00:02:31.165 --> 00:02:34.185
The kayak was just narrow enough to fit through our front door.

43
00:02:34.986 --> 00:02:37.066
We completed its construction in the open air.

44
00:02:37.086 --> 00:02:41.347
"That's a funny-looking boat," said little Franz.

45
00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:43.708
"Do you really think it will float?"

46
00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:45.848
"Look," said Fritz.

47
00:02:45.868 --> 00:02:48.909
"It's so light that I can pick it up with one hand."

48
00:02:48.929 --> 00:02:53.250
"It still seems awfully fragile to me," said my wife.

49
00:02:54.131 --> 00:02:58.832
Before she would allow him to try the kayak, she insisted on making him a special swimsuit.

50
00:02:59.584 --> 00:03:04.067
"I don't want him to drown if his boat is punctured by a sharp rock," she explained.

51
00:03:04.888 --> 00:03:09.291
"The kayak won't break like a soap bubble," I said with some exasperation.

52
00:03:10.112 --> 00:03:12.053
But I agreed to help her make the swimsuit.

53
00:03:12.894 --> 00:03:16.517
My wife said that Fritz needed a jacket, pants, and cap.

54
00:03:17.317 --> 00:03:21.120
We made these garments from linen and then lined them with another piece of fabric.

55
00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.782
Everything was then coated with rubber.

56
00:03:24.663 --> 00:03:29.635
We left a small hole, so that the garments could be inflated by blowing air between the linen

57
00:03:29.715 --> 00:03:30.355
and the lining.

58
00:03:31.296 --> 00:03:34.639
At last it was time for Fritz to take the kayak on a test voyage.

59
00:03:35.299 --> 00:03:36.580
We all gathered on the beach.

60
00:03:37.541 --> 00:03:41.144
I got out the canoe so my wife could see we were ready to rescue him if needed.

61
00:03:42.105 --> 00:03:45.027
Fritz stepped into the kayak and began to inflate his swimsuit.

62
00:03:45.748 --> 00:03:48.490
Fritz soon puffed up so that we could hardly recognize him.

63
00:03:49.211 --> 00:03:50.872
The boys shouted with laughter.

64
00:03:51.813 --> 00:03:53.794
Even my wife could not resist a smile.

65
00:03:53.814 --> 00:03:55.476
"You look so funny!"

66
00:03:56.409 --> 00:03:57.309
cried little Franz.

67
00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.293
The kayak floated lightly on the bay as Fritz began to paddle.

68
00:04:02.193 --> 00:04:03.694
First he darted straight ahead.

69
00:04:04.595 --> 00:04:07.077
Then he turned to the left and circled to the right.

70
00:04:07.918 --> 00:04:11.561
Finally he flipped on his side while his mother uttered a shriek of terror.

71
00:04:11.581 --> 00:04:13.702
"Oh no!"

72
00:04:14.043 --> 00:04:14.543
she cried.

73
00:04:15.043 --> 00:04:16.565
But Fritz quickly righted himself.

74
00:04:16.585 --> 00:04:18.166
"All is well!"

75
00:04:18.506 --> 00:04:20.188
he shouted to us over the water.

76
00:04:20.208 --> 00:04:23.810
"It may be just a tiny boat," I said to my wife.

77
00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.628
"But it's a sturdy one, and it won't sink."

78
00:04:27.469 --> 00:04:29.610
"Hooray for Fritz and the kayak!"

79
00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:30.530
yelled Jack.

80
00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.491
The other boys shouted their approval too.

81
00:04:34.292 --> 00:04:37.553
Fritz raised his arm in salute and turned the kayak away from shore.

82
00:04:38.394 --> 00:04:42.375
We watched him for a few minutes, and then suddenly I realized something dreadful.

83
00:04:43.476 --> 00:04:45.277
The tide was carrying him out to sea!

84
00:04:46.197 --> 00:04:47.157
"Ernest! Jack!"

85
00:04:47.397 --> 00:04:47.678
I said.

86
00:04:47.698 --> 00:04:49.498
"Help me launch the canoe.

87
00:04:49.879 --> 00:04:51.879
We must rescue your brother."

88
00:04:51.899 --> 00:04:53.000
We pushed off from shore.

89
00:04:53.832 --> 00:04:59.284
My wife wrapped her arms around little Franz and said, "I knew an accident would happen in that

90
00:04:59.405 --> 00:05:00.527
horrid soap bubble."
